{
  "id": "any-language",
  "title": "Many server languages",
  "summary": "Yon supports controllers in JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Java, Groovy, C#, F#, Kotlin, PHP, Rust, Dart, Go, Ruby, Lua and C++. Every language uses the same annotations, such as `RequestRoute`, `PostRoute` and `FromBody`. Tachyon reads the method signature and checks the request before the method runs. Here a body without `name` or with a text `level` gets 400. A model (a data type in `server/models/`) describes the body. JavaScript uses a JSDoc `@typedef` instead, Ruby types its method with YARD tags, Lua with LuaCATS comments, and C++ with its own types in `server/models/<Name>.hpp`. Tachyon prepares each controller, adapts it to the protocol and runs it under supervision. Under supervision, Tachyon watches the process and applies limits. A service in one of these languages uses `@Gateway` to call a class in another language. Every route also says who may call it, with `Public`, `SignedIn` or `Allow(Role)`, in every language.",
  "group": "Yon server",
